🇨🇦 The Ultimate Headless Live TV & DVR Stack
A Step-by-Step Guide for Jellyfin + Threadfin + Autoheal
This guide provides a stable, "Set and Forget" configuration for adding free, legal Live TV to Jellyfin using a headless Linux server.
📂 Phase 1: Directory & Permission Setup
First, create the "home" for your data. We use specific folders to separate your config files from your recordings and automation scripts.
 * Run this block in your terminal:
   # Create the folder structure
mkdir -p ~/live-tv-stack/{threadfin-config,scripts,recordings} && \

# Ensure your user owns these folders (Critical for Docker permissions)
sudo chown -R $USER:$USER ~/live-tv-stack && \

# Set read/write/execute permissions
chmod -R 755 ~/live-tv-stack && \

# Enter the project folder
cd ~/live-tv-stack

> 💡 Troubleshooting Tip: If you get a "Permission Denied" error later when Docker tries to save settings, re-run the sudo chown command above. It ensures Docker can "write" to your folders.
> 
🐳 Phase 2: Create the Docker Configuration
We use Docker Compose to manage two services: Threadfin (the tuner) and Autoheal (a watchdog that restarts Threadfin if it freezes).
 * Open the editor: nano docker-compose.yml
 * Paste this exact code:
<!-- end list -->
services:
  threadfin:
    image: fyb3roptik/threadfin:latest
    container_name: threadfin-standalone
    restart: unless-stopped
    # Injects your local user ID so you don't have permission issues
    user: "${UID_GID}" 
    ports:
      - "34400:34400"
    volumes:
      - ./threadfin-config:/home/threadfin/conf
    environment:
      - TZ=America/Toronto
    healthcheck:
      test: ["CMD", "wget", "-qO-", "http://localhost:34400/version"]
      interval: 2m
      timeout: 15s
      retries: 3
      start_period: 2m

  autoheal:
    image: willfarrell/autoheal
    container_name: autoheal
    restart: unless-stopped
    environment:
      - AUTOHEAL_CONTAINER_LABEL=all
    volumes:
      - /var/run/docker.sock:/var/run/docker.sock

(Press Ctrl+O, Enter, then Ctrl+X to save and exit.)
🚀 Phase 3: Launching the Stack
Because we are keeping the server secure, you must use sudo to launch. This command also "injects" your user ID into the container.
sudo UID_GID="$(id -u):$(id -g)" docker compose up -d

> 💡 Troubleshooting Tip: To check if it's actually running, type sudo docker ps. You should see both threadfin-standalone and autoheal listed.
> 
🇨🇦 Phase 4: Threadfin Configuration (The Web UI)
This is where the actual "tuning" happens. Do not just go to the IP address; you must use the /web/ suffix.
 * Find your IP: Type hostname -I | awk '{print $1}' in your terminal.
 * Access the Dashboard: Open http://[YOUR-IP]:34400/web/ in your browser.
 * The "Must-Do" Setting: Go to Settings > EPG Source. Change it to XEPG and click Save. If you skip this, Jellyfin will never see your channels.
 * Add Playlist: Go to Playlist > New.
   * M3U File: https://iptv-org.github.io/iptv/countries/ca.m3u.
 * Setup Filters: Go to Filters > New. Click the Group Title bar and select the categories you want (e.g., Entertainment, Movies, Documentaries).
📍 Phase 5: Manual Mapping (The Final Bridge)
Jellyfin cannot see your channels until they are "Mapped" and turn Green in Threadfin.
 * Open the Mapping Tab: You will see your filtered list of channels.
 * Pick Your Channels: Click an individual channel row.
 * Link to Guide: Select your XMLTV File and search for the matching XMLTV ID.
 * Make it Active: Ensure the "Active" box is checked. Once you click Done, the row must turn Green.
 * Verify: Look at your Threadfin dashboard. Under "Stream Information," Mapped Channels must be greater than 0.
🏒 Phase 6: Automated Commercial Skipping
 * Create the script: nano ~/live-tv-stack/scripts/comskip-clean.sh.
 * Paste the Logic:
<!-- end list -->
#!/bin/bash
FILEPATH="$1"
# Protect sports/hockey from being cut
if echo "$FILEPATH" | grep -Ei "Sports|Hockey|NHL|CFL"; then
    exit 0
fi
comskip --ini="/scripts/comskip.ini" "$FILEPATH"

 * Set Permissions: chmod +x ~/live-tv-stack/scripts/comskip-clean.sh.
🔗 Phase 7: Linking to Jellyfin
Now that Threadfin is "Green" and active, add the links to Jellyfin Dashboard > Live TV.
 * Tuner Device (+): Type: M3U Tuner | URL: http://[YOUR-IP]:34400/m3u/threadfin.m3u.
 * Guide Data (+): Type: XMLTV | URL: http://[YOUR-IP]:34400/xmltv/threadfin.xml.
 * DVR Settings:
   * Post-processor: /scripts/comskip-clean.sh.
   * Arguments: "{path}".
> 💡 Final Tip: If channels don't show up immediately, click Refresh Guide Data in Jellyfin. 
This triggers the system to pull the new "Green" channels from Threadfin.
